{
  "id": "ss.terrain.tunnel",
  "name": "Tunnel mouth (SS)",
  "description": "Shape Survivors set dressing: a hole dug up through the field from below, and the same hole caved in. The spoil is heaped highest on the near lip where it was pushed out, and it is warm turned earth rather than the ruins' purple stone — the one ring on this ground that means dug, not built. Drawn at the crater tilt the pheromone vent uses, so a mouth cut into open flats and one cut into a burrow chamber read as the same object. Set into the lip is a ring of fourteen husk teeth leaning in over the throat, each hooked the same way round and each sized by one fixed roll, so fourteen of them read as grown rather than cut. They are laid out on the un-tilted circle and projected with it, which is what foreshortens them: the pair at the sides stand at full length while the ones on the near and far lips are seen nearly end-on, the same way the hole itself is. And they are the warning the thing otherwise has no room for \u2014 nothing announces a tunnel, so a mouth that takes a bite out of whoever drops through it has to say so before they do. The `filled` variant is what a spent tunnel leaves: the heap gone back down the hole, domed and paler than the ground it came out of, broken into clods on top and sunk away from the lip where it settled.",
